# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
CapIQ Insurance Investment Holdings -> PowerBI-ready tables (v2)

Source screen: 
  Life/Fraternal | Individual Cos | Private Placement = Yes

Real export layout (sheet '26q1'):
  Row 2/3: main header text (merged cells -> only first cell of each pair filled)
  Row 4:   field IDs
  Row 5:   period (mixed: 2024Y/2025Y for values, 2025Q4/2026Q1 for
           NAIC Designation / SVO Symbol / NAIC Schedule / Conditional FV)
  Row 6+:  data

Outputs one xlsx with two sheets:
  1. Fact_Holdings (long): one row per holding x snapshot year (2024 / 2025).
     NA Carrying Value for a year = not held that year -> dropped.
     NAIC buckets (1/2/3-6/Not Designated) + SVO buckets
     (PL / No Symbol / FE / Other admin states) + sort keys; designation/SVO
     use each snapshot's own year when present (fallback 2025Q4, logged).
     2026Q1 designation/SVO kept as *_Latest columns (migration analysis).
     CUSIP_Type: dataset is 100% PPN (special chars *,@,# are PPN-only) -
     'PPN (issuer-level)' (char in pos 6) vs 'PPN (issue-level)' (pos 7-8,
     private deal of a CUSIP'd public issuer); any 'Standard' -> WARN.
  2. Dim_Entity: one row per entity; PP Bonds % of Total Bonds / of C&S
     (2026Q1, from CapIQ) aggregated from holding rows; group / rating /
     denominators joined from optional ENTITY_FILE, placeholders otherwise.

KNOWN CAVEATS (keep in dashboard footnotes):
  - Universe = Sched D Pt 1 membership AS OF 2026Q1 -> survivorship bias in
    prior-year snapshots; YoY = growth of surviving book.
  - 144A NOT in dataset (flag = PPN universe); FE bucket = publicly rated
    traditional private placements, not 144A.
  - Sched BA (funds/direct lending) & Sched B (mortgage loans) not covered.

Carrying Value (BACV) is the primary exposure metric; $000 -> $.
% metrics are DAX measures in Power BI. Never label totals "Total" -
use "PP BACV (Sched D Pt 1)".
"""

import os
import re
import sys

import numpy as np
import pandas as pd

# --- CONFIGURATION -----------------------------------------------------
